  "turn_number": 2,
  "player_text": "I turn northwest from the board and look for the old crates and the muddy track the posting names, trying to see how far that route sits from the gate and whether anyone is already heading that way.",
  "visible_motivation": "The missing patrol was last sent that way this morning, and the ink is still damp.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want to spot the track and the crates so I can judge whether I can look into the patrol before the dusk curfew.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "Turning northwest from the notice board, you spot the old crates stacked beside a muddy track winding away from the gate. The worn path leads through a tangle of damp underbrush, its ruts deep and slick from recent rains. The track lies roughly a few dozen paces from the eastern gate’s choke point, veering into quieter terrain beyond the bustling gate district. You can see no one currently heading out along the track, but the faint sounds of movement hint that the path is still in use, perhaps by those aiming to avoid the crowded official entry. The missing patrol’s route, as named on the board, likely took this muddy way past the crates northwest.",
